    },
    {
      "title": "Filter solutions by their own case",
      "body": "<p>Solve the resulting equation in each region, then retain only roots satisfying that region’s restrictions.</p>",
      "recap": "Splitting at a modulus formula change allows each area to be calculated using its correct linear pieces.",
      "pitfall": "A root of a case formula need not be a solution of the original problem outside that case.",
